7,(PDF) A brief outline of Chen phonology,https://www.academia.edu/73299396/A_brief_outline_of_Chen_phonology,"The Tangsa language belongs to the Sino-Tibetan family of languages. It is spoken by the Tangsa people of Myanmar and North-eastern India.2 Chen is listed as Naga, Chen-Kayu by Ethnologue (Eberhard et al., 2021). This study includes only Chen data, no Kayu data.","Naga, Chen-Kayu",Sino-Tibetan
